{"step_index":123,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T13:45:46Z","input_tokens":2833,"cache_read_tokens":122095,"output_tokens":3186,"content":"Here is a critical review of the plan against the iOS and Desktop implementations, highlighting bugs in the initial draft, subtle UIKit edge cases, and refinements needed before implementation.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Bugs & Edge Cases in the Initial Plan\n\n#### A. Combine Dirty-Flag Bug (Section E)\n* **Issue in plan**:\n  ```swift\n  self?.requestContentRender(transcript: self?.mode.selectedSegmentIndex == ConversationMode.liveText.rawValue)\n  ```\n  If a reaction arrives while the user is on the **Chat** tab (or while the panel/app is backgrounded), `transcriptDirty` remains `false`. Later, when `viewDidAppear` runs (which calls `requestContentRender(messages: false, transcript: false)`), it relies on `transcriptDirty` already being `true`.\n* **Fix**:\n  [`requestContentRender()`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/RockNRoll/ConversationPanelViewController.swift#L711-L734) *already* defers `renderTranscript()` until `mode == .liveText`, `contentVisible`, and `contentIsActive`.\n  - In `chat.reactionHistory.$events` (line 211), simply call `self?.requestContentRender()` (both `messages: true` and `transcript: true`). It costs zero renders while on `.chat` and guarantees `transcriptDirty` is set.\n  - Also update `chat.$reactionHistoryAvailable` (line 221) so it doesn't pass `transcript: false`.\n\n#### B. Undated `TranscriptSegment`s & the `first` Cutoff (Section B)\n* **Issue in plan**:\n  1. In `liveTextRows()`, initializing `var last = Date.distantPast` assigns `Date.distantPast` (`0001-01-01`) to any leading undated `TranscriptSegment` (`spokenAt == nil`).\n  2. `if let first = rows.first?.0` then evaluates to `Date.distantPast`, which breaks the `event.timestamp >= first` filter and pulls in reactions from before the first dated segment, while sorting all undated segments before all reactions.\n  3. In [`CatchUpTimeline.precedes`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/ConferenceCore/Sources/ConferenceCore/CatchUpTimeline.swift#L110-L117), undated segments (`spokenAt == nil`) are actually placed at the *end* of `timeline.segments` (after dated segments).\n* **Fix**:\n  - Derive the reaction cutoff `first` from the earliest *dated* segment (`timeline.segments.lazy.compactMap(\\.spokenAt).first`).\n  - Keep `segment.spokenAt` (`Date?`) inside `.line(TranscriptSegment)` for display so `Date.distantPast` is never formatted as a visible timestamp string.\n\n#### C. Empty-Transcript State & `UITextView` Attribute Bleed (Section D)\n* **Issue in plan**:\n  1. **Reactions before speech**: If `canViewTranscript == true && transcriptionEnabled` and reactions arrive *before* anyone speaks (`timeline.segments.isEmpty`), Desktop shows the empty-state prompt (\"Transcript appears here...\") *and* lists the reactions below it. On iOS, if we render when `!rows.isEmpty`, we should still include the header/status note (`\"Text received by this phone may be incomplete.\"`, plus `\"Waiting for spoken words…\"` if `timeline.segments.isEmpty`).\n  2. **`UITextView` attribute bleed**: Previously, the last character of `liveTranscript()` was always `line.text` (`.body`, `.white`), which matched `transcript`'s default font/color. If the last row is now a `.reaction` (`.caption1`, `.lightGray`) and the room later resets to the plain-text `else` branch (`transcript.text = message`), `UITextView` will inherit `.caption1` / `.lightGray` from the previous `attributedText`!\n* **Fix**:\n  - Always reset `transcript.font = .preferredFont(forTextStyle: .body)` and `transcript.textColor = .white` (or set `transcript.attributedText`) in the fallback `else` branch of `renderTranscript()`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Formatting & Behavior Refinements\n\n#### A. Single-Line Alignment in `UITextView` (Section C)\n* On Desktop (SwiftUI), a reaction row uses `HStack { emoji; name; Spacer(); time }`.\n* On iOS, [`transcriptLines`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/RockNRoll/ConversationPanelViewController.swift#L926-L944) renders into a single `UITextView` with leading timestamps:\n  ```text\n  14:05  Alex\n  Hello everyone\n  ```\n* To align cleanly in `UITextView` without a right-aligned tab stop, format reaction rows with the same leading timestamp pattern:\n  ```text\n  14:06  👍  Alex\n  ```\n  - Timestamp: `\"\\(event.timestamp.formatted(date: .omitted, time: .shortened))  \"` (`.caption1`, `.lightGray`)\n  - Reaction + Name: `\"\\(event.kind.emoji)  \\(name)\"` (`.caption1`, `.lightGray`)\n  - For `name`, use `event.isOwn ? L(\"You\") : (event.displayName ?? L(\"Participant\"))` to match [`ReactionHistoryRowView`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/RockNRoll/ReactionHistoryRowView.swift#L42) and [`messageRow`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/RockNRoll/ConversationPanelViewController.swift#L840).\n\n#### B. Incremental `textStorage` Appending (Section D)\n* `MeetingReactionEvent` can mutate in place when `resolveUnknownParticipant` or `acknowledge` updates an existing event.\n* Because both `TranscriptSegment` and `MeetingReactionEvent` conform to `Equatable`, `LiveTextRow: Equatable` with `rows.starts(with: previous)` will automatically detect any in-place mutation or out-of-order insertion in earlier rows and fall back to a full `transcript.attributedText` rebuild, while still fast-path appending when new lines or reactions arrive at the tail.\n\n#### C. Unseen Reaction State (`markVisibleReactions`)\n* Keep [`markVisibleReactions()`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/RockNRoll/ConversationPanelViewController.swift#L813-L827) scoped to `.chat` mode so viewing `Live text` does not alter unread reaction badges or break existing `ReactionHistoryPanelTests` contracts.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Scope Check: Catch Up Tab?\nIn Desktop commit `678cb5c`, reactions were added to both **Live text** and **Catch up** interval cards (`DesktopMeetingModel.catchUpReactions(_:)`). On iOS, [`CatchUpCardsView`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/RockNRoll/CatchUpCardsView.swift) currently only displays `TranscriptSegment`s.\n\nWould you like me to proceed with implementing the refined **Live text** plan above (or also include reactions in **Catch up** cards)?","thinking":"The code references a `recordLocalSubmission` function within the `NativeConferenceEngine`. This function appears to be logging or recording some sort of submission related to chat reactions. Further investigation into the specific parameters and their context within the larger code structure is necessary to understand the exact purpose and potential issues.\n\n\nThe code consistently uses `\"You\"` when displaying the current user's reactions in chat, regardless of platform or view. There's a discrepancy in how other participants are referenced, sometimes defaulting to a generic \"Participant\" label if their display name is unavailable. The iOS views maintain consistent use of `\"You\"` for the user's reactions, mirroring the desktop behavior.\n\n\nReview of the plan needs to address the lack of live transcription reactions in the iOS Catch Up view, contrasting with the desktop application's behavior. The review should explicitly note this discrepancy and determine if the iOS implementation is intentionally different or if parity is desired. The proposed fix, a direct call to `requestContentRender()`, should resolve the subscription dirty-flag bug.\n\n\nThe initial hypothesis points to rendering deferral based on the mode and visibility. Also, the `transcript: false` flag should be removed from the reaction history availability check.\n\nUndated transcript segments in the `CatchUpTimeline` are sorted after dated segments, which causes the initial undated segments to bypass the filtering logic due to an incorrect initialization. The fix involves determining